As a Production Operator, you will work with different machines and make sure the glass is processed correctly. Operating and setting up production machines; 
Carrying out quality checks; 
Checking that the production process is running correctly; 
Taking on more responsibility within the production process. 
You will work an average of 38 hours per week in a 3-shift schedule. The shifts rotate between early, late and night shifts: 05:30-14:00, 14:00-22:30 and 22:30-05:30. On Fridays, the late shift ends at 23:00. The night shift starts earlier on Sunday evening because the machines need to be started. 15.92 gross per hour plus a 23% shift allowance, giving you €19.58 gross per hour; 
~€Full-time position with an average of 38 hours per week; 
~ Temporary contract with the possibility of a permanent contract; 
~ Choice between weekly or four-weekly salary payments; 
~ Free fresh fruit every day; 
~ For this position, we are looking for someone who already has production experience and wants to keep learning. Are available full-time; 
Are willing to work in 3 shifts; 
Have experience in a production environment; 
Work accurately and care about quality; 
Speak German, English or Dutch. 
Experience with production machines is a plus. Over het bedrijf 
At Scheuten in Venlo, glass is processed and worked on for different applications, from homes and hotels to large buildings and special projects. 
You will work in a modern production environment with an international team. Do you already have production experience, enjoy working with machines and want to develop yourself further? Apply today as a Production Operator at Scheuten in Venlo!

Are you looking for a fulltime job in logistics? Would you like to work in a modern, international warehouse where fashion and clothing products are shipped to customers all over the world? Then this opportunity could be perfect for you!

For a large logistics clothing warehouse in Lelystad, we are looking for motivated Production Workers, Warehouse Operatives, and Logistics Associates. You will become part of a friendly international team where teamwork, quality, and a positive working atmosphere are key. On top of that, you can enjoy a delicious hot lunch every working day.

As a Production Worker in the warehouse, you will help ensure that all goods are processed efficiently and accurately. Your tasks will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking and packing customer orders;
- Checking products for quality;
- Unpacking boxes and processing incoming goods;
- Sorting clothing and accessories;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

This is a full-time position in a 2-shift rotation:

- Morning shift: 07:00 AM - 03:30 PM
- Afternoon shift: 03:00 PM - 11:30 PM

But there is also a nightshift you can work if you want from 23:00 tot 07:30. And there is work in the weekends!

- (Basic) English communication skills, or Polish or Spanish;
- Availability for full-time work in a 2-shift schedule;
- Ability to work effectively in a team;
- Physically fit and comfortable performing active warehouse work;
- Attention to detail and ability to follow instructions;
- Previous logistics or warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

Are you an experienced Reach Truck Driver looking for a new opportunity? We are currently recruiting for a modern logistics company in Helmond. As a Reach Truck Driver, you will be responsible for safely and efficiently moving goods throughout the warehouse while supporting daily logistics operations using modern equipment.

Your responsibilities:

- Operating a reach truck at heights of up to 12 meters;
- Moving and storing pallets throughout the warehouse;
- Picking orders using the reach truck;
- Scanning, labeling, and wrapping pallets;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Supporting Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule may be required. (6:00-15:00/15:00-00:00)

- Holds a valid Reach Truck certificate;
- Is comfortable working at heights up to 12 meters;
- Fulltime available;
- Living nearby Helmond, Mierlo, Geldrop, Nuenen or Eindhoven;
- Has experience in logistics and safety;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English.

In the role of Quality Control Specialist, you will take charge of preserving product quality at every step of the production cycle. Your key responsibilities involve:
- Carrying out precise measurements and sampling in line with predefined standards;
- Reviewing and authorizing product batches prior to their transfer to storage;
- Overseeing and ensuring quality consistency throughout different production phases;
- Conducting quality assessments based on the established quality plan;
- Ensuring defective products do not proceed into the supply chain.

 - Work full-time in a rotating 5-shift pattern (06:00–14:00, 14:00–22:00, 22:00–06:00);
- Earn a competitive salary of €3,236 monthly, which includes a 28.5% shift bonus;
- Receive a travel reimbursement of €0.23 per kilometer, with no upper limit;
- Access various opportunities to grow personally and professionally within the organization;
- Start saving for your pension from day one under Covebo;
- Enjoy 25 vacation days provided through Covebo;
- Benefit from an 8.33% holiday bonus via Covebo;
- Explore the chance to secure a permanent role with Canpack after your time with Covebo.

 - Excellent command of English, both verbal and written;
- Hands-on experience with tools and methods for quality assurance;
- Exceptional analytical abilities and attention to detail;
- Familiarity with safety protocols and hygiene standards;
- Skilled in using Microsoft Office programs.

 For over 30 years, Canpack Helmond has been a leader in the metal packaging industry. With a strong presence in Central and Eastern Europe and expanding into Western Europe, Asia, and Africa, they are one of the largest manufacturers of metal packaging worldwide. Their dedicated team of nearly 8,000 employees produces approximately 25 billion beverage cans, 28 billion bottle closures, 1 billion metal containers for the food and chemical industries, and 700 tons of glass packaging annually.
